# Nightly: the service database name does not match the one the job uses.
#
# WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
# --------------------
# The Nightly job on main FAILED on 2026-11-18 (run 44404490001, SHA
# 7c0c53ce). The failing step was the "Nightly reset" job, and the
# error was:
#
#     FATAL:  database "gustale_ci" does not exist
#
# THE CAUSE
# ----------
# The service container was told to create a database called
# `gustale_ci_ci`:
#
#     .github/workflows/nightly.yml:49
#       POSTGRES_DB: gustale_ci_ci
#
# but the job connects to `gustale_ci` in two places:
#
#     .github/workflows/nightly.yml:14
#       DATABASE_URL: postgres://gustale:...@127.0.0.1:5432/gustale_ci
#     .github/workflows/nightly.yml:105
#       PGPASSWORD=gustale psql -h 127.0.0.1 -U postgres -d gustale_ci ...
#
# So the container created one database and the job asked for another.
# The `_ci` suffix looks like a copy/paste slip: `ci.yml` runs its own
# service with `POSTGRES_DB: gustale_ci`, and the Nightly was given
# the name with `_ci` appended.
#
# WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT A COMMIT
# ----------------------------------
# The GitHub App this repository is pushed with has NO `workflows`
# scope, so it cannot push a change to `.github/workflows/*.yml` at
# all -- GitHub rejects the token with 422. The owner has to apply
# this by hand.
#
# HOW TO APPLY
# ------------
#     git checkout main
#     git apply docs/ci-nightly-postgres-db.patch
#     git commit -m "ci: the nightly service database is gustale_ci"
#     git push
#
# After it lands, the Nightly's own service container will create
# `gustale_ci`, which is the database both the reset step and the
# migration chain already use.
#
# THE ONE-LINE FIX
# ----------------
#     -          POSTGRES_DB: gustale_ci_ci
#     +          POSTGRES_DB: gustale_ci
#
diff --git a/.github/workflows/nightly.yml b/.github/workflows/nightly.yml
--- a/.github/workflows/nightly.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/nightly.yml
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
           # the chain applies the migrations.
           POSTGRES_USER: postgres
           POSTGRES_PASSWORD: gustale
-          POSTGRES_DB: gustale_ci_ci
+          POSTGRES_DB: gustale_ci
         ports:
           - 5432:5432
         options: >-
